Package: incantation
Title: Post-Layout Graphics Manipulation for R
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Incantation", "Authors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "mackenzie_quiwck@programmer.net")
Description: A post-layout visual editing layer for 'ggplot2', 'patchwork',
    'aplot' and 'cowplot' figures. Once a composition has been laid out,
    incantation selects whole subplots or individual graphical elements and
    moves, aligns or restacks them without recomputing the layout: canvas size,
    panel dimensions, sibling positions and row/column weights stay frozen.
    Every measurement is reported in device points against an explicitly bound
    device size, and every edit is a structured, serialisable operation, so an
    agent can measure a gap, act on it, and verify the result in a closed loop.
    Result-native SVG snapshots additionally expose individual circles, text,
    paths and other visible primitives for structured leaf-level editing and
    fixed-size pixel verification without inspecting the plotting process.
